    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0193" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg131"/>

                <head>No. 87.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Holcombe to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 20, 1878</date>.
                        (Received August 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to hand to you herewith a
                    copy of an interesting dispatch recently received from the vice-consul at New
                    Chwang. It is not yet known what steps, if any, the French Government propose to
                    take in the premises.</p>
                <p>Rumors are current here of coming difficulty between Corea and Japan, but they
                    can be traced to no reliable source.</p>
                <p>Any further information which I may obtain will be promptly communicated.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHESTER HOLCOMBE</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d92-a1.xml" xpointer="d92-a1"/>
            </div>
